# WHAT IT COVERS: the first of two 2026-11-14 streams, 110.1 minutes cut to the gameplay its
# video shows, captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with o:vsync on d4d6001, the step
# tolerance at 18% and the long-gap rule at 100 ms, the same launch as 2026-11-13. It carries
# step_tolerance_pct 18. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 1296 times (706 an hour) and stalled for
# 100 ms or more 143 times (78 an hour), in 217 bursts, 74 of them with a stall; the longest
# stalls are 591 ms at about 4644 s, 545 ms at about 2791 s and 525 ms at about 4282 s. No
# periodic stretch. The lock released 10 times. The worst blend run, 30 presents in the field,
# starts at 4225.59 s beside a 42 ms hitch and a lock release at 4225.65 s.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 47.436 s, from the 2589
# marked frames in its first 43 s, matched within 0.41 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 6608.0 s with no holes; it opens on gameplay and the map and ends on the pause menu, which
# opens at video time 6605.5 s, so the cut is 47.4 s to 6652.9 s. Inside the cut, 34 seconds in
# 34 runs fall out of the 60 fps regime, each a single hitch second.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships (the split-pair rule added since is off
# by default and off here), with the step tolerance at the setting the key names, so the two
# lines are comparable. The replay line (the plain arm, no dejitter) reads synth 1.6% against
# 1.7%, worst run 22 against 30, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 222 against 222. On the
# dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, synth 1.6% and the worst run 29, starting at the
# same present as the field's 30, hence max_worst_run_dejit 29 beside the plain arm's 22.
# Counted over the window, replay against field: synthesized presents 6520 against 6536,
# repeats 1312 against 1311, skips 593 against 591. The replay makes 45 moves, 12 of them late,
# and 12 land more than 2 ms from a real frame; the field made 45 inside the window. The lock
# released 10 times in the field and 9 on the replay, the 9 within 0.47 ms; the field's tenth,
# at 3571.50 s, lasts two presents after a lock move and a 26 ms hitch, and the replay holds
# the lock there. The planner at 100 ms draws 797 synthesized presents over 164 pairs as the
# blend; the field drew 802 over the same 164 pairs.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
